                <p>A method and apparatus are provided for controlling a display device (215) to generate an image for viewing by a user on a head or helmet-mounted display, HMD, the display device having pixel-sized elements each separately controllable to reflect, emit or transmit light from one or more illuminating light sources, the image being formed by three light components displayed sequentially in three respective phases having predetermined relative timings defining equal time intervals between the respective phases in which the three light components are to be displayed, each light component comprising either a period of continuous illumination by one of said pixel-sized elements or a period comprising a set of light pulses according to a pulse width modulation, PWM, scheme, the method comprising the steps:(i) at an apparatus for controlling the display device, receiving image data defining three light components of a feature to be displayed as an element in the image;(ii) at said apparatus, receiving rate data indicative of a rate of change in orientation of the display relative to a direction of gaze of an eye (220) of the user (205), and receiving orientation data indicative of an orientation of the HMD in inertial space;(iii) at an image processor (245) of said apparatus, determining a position on the display for displaying each of the three light components of the feature including determining any respective adjustment required to a determined position for the light component according to the received rate data and the predetermined relative timings; and(iv) at the image processor (245) of said apparatus, outputting the determined position of each of the three light components to the display device for display of the light component at the respective determined position,wherein for the first and third light components to be displayed of the three light components, at step (iii) said respective adjustment is determined using the timing of the phase in which the light component is to be displayed relative to the timing of the phase in which the second light component to be displayed of the three light components is to be displayed, and at step (iv) the determined position of the light component including said respective adjustment is outputted to the display device;wherein at step (iii) no adjustment is required to the determined position of the second light component, such that at step (iv) the determined position of the second light component is outputted to the display device without any adjustment;wherein for the first and third light components, at step (iii) the respective adjustment is determined based on the difference in time, Δt, between the phase in which said one of the first or third light components is to be displayed and the phase in which the second light component is to be displayed, and based on respective rates of rotation about y and z axes of the display device, ry and rz.</p>
